(4) Biggest win: blur the sticky bar only once content is behind it. Move `backdrop-filter` and `-webkit-backdrop-filter` from `.topbar` to `.topbar.is-scrolled { ... }` and add to settings.js and app.js:
```js
const topbar = document.querySelector('.topbar');
const syncTopbar = () => topbar.classList.toggle('is-scrolled', window.scrollY > 0);
window.addEventListener('scroll', syncTopbar, { passive: true });
syncTopbar();
```
At scrollY 0 only the flat page background is behind the bar (diff at most 7/255 on under 0.01% of pixels). If the owner wants the glow that body::before was meant to draw, restore it with the missing commas and without the blur; that is a visible change.

